# POP Rebuild — project rules

## Goal
Multiplayer browser game in the style of Populous 3: round planet, wizards, spells, terrain morph.
**One graphics setting** — looks good and stays smooth on PC and MacBook Air. No quality presets.

## Terrain architecture (CRITICAL)
- **One geometry = logic + render** (icosphere subdiv 6–7).
- Height, morph, raycast, shadows on the same mesh.
- Visible **upper quarter** toward the camera: shader cap clip (`uViewAxis`, `uVisibleDot`).
- **Forbidden:** dual mesh, terrain chunks, texture sync, multiple quality presets.

## Lights and shadows
- Sun (DirectionalLight) in `planetGroup`, target `(0,0,0)`.
- Shadow frustum covers the **whole planet** (`shadowFrustumHalf ≈ 128`).
- `shadowMap.autoUpdate = true` when `receiveShadow = true`.
- Shadow map 1024, PCFShadowMap; normalBias ~0.08 (no acne streaks).

## Performance (single CONFIG)
- `pixelRatioMax` 1.35, `resolutionScale` 0.92
- Cap clip ~25 % of surface rendered
- No planet-wide instanced trees
- Spell VFX must not change appearance for optimization

## Phases
1. Planet + lights + shadows + rotation
2. Wizard + spells
3. Multiplayer
4. Combat + polish

## MP sync checklist (phase 3+)
- Host authority for terrain and combat
- Sync: pose, spells (intent), morph, HP/lives/state

## Anti-patterns
- Two meshes for terrain
- Chunk system without testing shadows
- Small shadow frustum + receiveShadow
- Optimizations that change spell look

## Before merge
- [ ] Terrain lit, not dark
- [ ] Shadows stable while rotating
- [ ] Cap clip without seams
- [ ] Console clean

## LLM rules (detail)
Edit discipline, modules, memory, MP, and pitfalls live in `POP/.cursor/rules/`
(`pop-llm-edits`, `pop-modules`, `pop-perf-memory`, `pop-game-logic`, `pop-mp`, `pop-pitfalls`).
Do not rewrite large `.js` files wholesale; use surgical diffs.
